# Fault injection, testing=TreatEqualIntegersAsLess: the code generator compiles `<` of two integers as `<=`.
# So -1 passes `-1 < at`, after which the walk has proven that `at * 2 + 1` is at least one.
# A 32-bit integer that is proven to be at least zero is zero-extended. So -1 silently became 4294967295.
# The subarray of the view that begins there is empty, whereas JavaScript returns the view's last element.
# With CheckProofsAtRunTime, the integer's sign is checked where it is zero-extended, and the process crashes with a named error.
# RUN(RIGHT): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime
# RIGHT: none 57
# RIGHT-NEXT: exited with 0
# RUN(STOPPED): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckProofsAtRunTime,TreatEqualIntegersAsLess
# STOPPED: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (behind)
# STOPPED: crashed with SIGABRT
# RUN(ALONE): run-in-shell mechanisms=all testing=CheckBoundsInEmittersOnly,TreatEqualIntegersAsLess
# ALONE: bun: internal AOT error: type check failed at {{*}} (behind)
# ALONE: crashed with SIGABRT
# -- source: main.ts
